Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Stop the hero's three facts from looking like buttons
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

They were bordered pills sitting ABOVE the call to action, so the first thing
the page offered was three things shaped like buttons that do nothing, followed
by the two that actually go somewhere. Nobody could tell which was which.

The facts are a caption, so they now look like one — plain text with a tinted
icon, no border, no background — and they sit below the buttons rather than in
front of them. On a narrow screen they stack into a short list instead of
wrapping into three ragged lines.

"For organizers" is green rather than outlined. Beside a filled crimson button
an outlined one reads as a caption too, and half the audience for this page is
the organizer who needs to see that a second door exists.

The sub-headline also stopped promising bank transfer alone on a site where
organizers take PayPal — it follows the same live check as the rest of the page.

